      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\n/*\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\n */\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \n * the system.\n */\nvoid body_force(Body * restrict p, float dt, int n) {\n  #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    float fx = 0.0f; \n    float fy = 0.0f; \n    float fz = 0.0f;\n\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n      float dx = p[j].x - p[i].x;\n      float dy = p[j].y - p[i].y;\n      float dz = p[j].z - p[i].z;\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3; \n      fy += dy * inv_dist3; \n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    p[i].vx += dt*fx; \n    p[i].vy += dt*fy; \n    p[i].vz += dt*fz;\n\n    // Fuse position update into the same parallel region to reduce barrier overhead.\n    p[i].x += p[i].vx * DT;\n    p[i].y += p[i].vy * DT;\n    p[i].z += p[i].vz * DT;\n  }\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\n */\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  /*\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\n   */\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\n    body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(bodies);\n  \n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Fusing the position update into the force computation loop eliminates one OpenMP parallel region and its implicit barrier per simulation iteration, reducing thread synchronization overhead while preserving exact floating-point semantics because each body's velocity is updated before its own position in the same sequential order as the original two-loop version.",
  "notes": "The transformation keeps all arithmetic operations and their order identical to the baseline: forces are accumulated sequentially over j, then velocities are updated with dt*fx etc., and positions use the newly computed velocity multiplied by DT. Since each i is handled by exactly one thread, there is no cross-thread dependency on the position update. This should reduce per-iteration overhead without changing output bytes.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Fused the separate position-update loop into body_force's parallel for region",
    "Removed the second #pragma omp parallel for from main"
  ]
